body:
> Solutions to achieve this use-case: add a VirtualWidget with the slug param as the defaultRefinement.

This solution looks like a workaround (good one). But still in react I would expect that updating any prop on InstantSearch would actually do what I want: update the corresponding linked behaviors. What do you think?

Ultimately we might just have a state with:

```
searchParameters: {
  page: 0,
  filters: ...
  distinct: ...
},
widgets: {
  menu: {
    brands: 'Sony'
  }
}
```

But in the meantime, what about we allow updating searchParameters?

And users will be able to update any searchParameters (sorry this is confusing, I am not really talking about SearchParameters from the helper here, just all API parameters that are not handled by widgets.)
